{"id":"G1342","lemma":"δίκαιος","transliteration":"dikaios","sayIt":"dikaios","language":"Greek","partOfSpeech":"adjective","gloss":"just","meaning":"δίκαιος, -α, -ον\n(δίκη), [in LXX chiefly for צַדִּיק (for rendering of צַדִּיק in sense of correct, see Deiss., BS, 115 f.); sometimes for נָקִי as Pro.1:11, al. ;]\nin early Gk. writers\n(a) of persons, observant of δίκη, custom, rule, right, righteous in performing duties to gods and men ;\n(b) of things, righteous, in accordance with right.\nIn NT\n1. righteous, chiefly in the broad sense, as above, of the person or thing corresponding to the Divine standard of right\n(a) of persons: of God, Rom.3:26, 1Jn.2:29 Jn 3:7; of Christ, Act.3:14 7:52 22:14, 1Pe.3:18, 1Jn.2:1; of men, Mat.1:19 (Abbott, Essays, 75 f.) Mat.10:41 13:17, 43 13:49, Luk.1:6, 17, Rom.5:7, 1Ti.1:9, Jas.5:6, 1Pe.3:12, 1Jn.3:7, Rev.22:11, al.; δ. καὶ εὐλαβής, Luk.2:25; ἅγιος, Mrk.6:20; ἀγαθός, Luk.23:50; φοβούμενος τ. θεόν, Act.10:22; opposite to ἀμαρτωλοὶ καὶ ἀσεβεῖς, 1Pe.4:18; ἄδικοι, Mat.5:45, Act.24:15; δ. ἐκ πίστεως, Rom.1:17, Gal.3:11, Heb.10:38\" (LXX) ; δ. παρὰ τ. θεῷ, Rom.2:13\n(b) of things: ἔργα δ., opposite to πονηρὰ, 1Jn.3:12; ἐντολή, Rom.7:12; metaphorically, αἷμα, Mat.23:35; τὸ δ., Luk.12:57; δ. ἐστιν, Act.4:19, Eph.6:1, Php.1:7; ὅ, Mat.20:4; ὅσα, Php.4:8\n2. In narrower sense\n(a) of persons, as in later cl. writers, just, rendering to each his due: Tit.1:8, 1Jn.1:9; δ. κριτής, 2Ti.4:8\n(b) of things: τὸ δ., Col.4:1; δ., sc. ἐστιν, 2Th.1:6; κρίσις δ., Jhn.5:30; ὁδοί, Rev.15:3\nSYN.: ἀγαθός (which see), καλός, χρηστός (Cremer, 183, 690). (AS)","glosses":["righteous","right","righteous man","just","righteous one","righteous men"],"count":74,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"mat-1","v":19,"renderings":{"bsb":"a righteous man","kjv":"a just"}},{"chapterId":"mat-5","v":45,"renderings":{"bsb":"the righteous","kjv":"the just"}},{"chapterId":"mat-9","v":13,"renderings":{"bsb":"the righteous","kjv":"the righteous"}},{"chapterId":"mat-10","v":41,"re