 but those who are sick. I came not to call the righteous, but…","source":"web"},{"ref":"Luke 1:6","note":"They were both righteous before God, walking blamelessly in all the commandments and ordinances of the Lord.","source":"web"},{"ref":"John 5:30","note":"I can of myself do nothing. As I hear, I judge, and my judgment is righteous; because I don’t seek my own will, but the will of my Father who sent me.","source":"web"},{"ref":"Acts 3:14","note":"But you denied the Holy and Righteous One and asked for a murderer to be granted to you,","source":"web"},{"ref":"Romans 1:17","note":"For in it is revealed God’s righteousness from faith to faith. As it is written, “But the righteous shall live by faith.”","source":"web"},{"ref":"Galatians 3:11","note":"Now that no man is justified by the law before God is evident, for, “The righteous will live by faith.”","source":"web"},{"ref":"Ephesians 6:1","note":"Children, obey your parents in the Lord, for this is right.","source":"web"}],"related":[{"id":"G1343","lemma":"δικαιοσύνη","transliteration":"dikaiosunē","gloss":"righteousness"}],"sources":["STEPBible TBESH/TBESG lexicon (CC BY 4.0)","STEPBible TAHOT/TAGNT tagged text (CC BY 4.0)"]}